{"id":2703,"date":"2021-03-01T18:26:21","date_gmt":"2021-03-02T02:26:21","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=2703"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:37:43","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:37:43","slug":"windows-pycharm-installation-and-setup","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/windows-pycharm-installation-and-setup\/","title":{"rendered":"Windows PyCharm Installation and Setup"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215732c0e7\" name=\"6a2215732c0e7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Install PyCharm Edu<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You are going to install <a href=\"https:\/\/www.jetbrains.com\/pycharm-edu\/\">PyCharm Edu<\/a>, which is what you&#8217;ll use for programing CoDrone. PyCharm is what many actual Python programmers use![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/youtu.be\/ZC3bY5BNzQI&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215732c20b\" name=\"6a2215732c20b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>PyCharm environment setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this video, you will create a new project, link it to your Python interpreter that you just installed, and install the right CoDrone library.[\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=NdjgoBG_iG8&#8243; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215732c276\" name=\"6a2215732c276\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Test flight<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]To make su